Subject: [PATCH] touchscreen-menu: do not read the layout row past its eight
 entries

TouchscreenMenu_LoadSpriteResources loads TOUCHSCREEN_MENU_NUM_RESOURCES
(11) resource slots through TouchscreenMenu_LoadIconResources. Slots 0-6 are
the layout icons and 7-10 are the item/button/ball slots, but the function
reads gTouchscreenMenuLayouts[layout][index] before its index-specific
branches, so slots 8-10 read past the eight bytes of the row. On the DS that
lands in the next row (harmless bss); on the host UBSan reports "index 8 out
of bounds for type u8 [8]".

Under SDK_PORT_3DS, read the layout only inside the row and use
TOUCHSCREEN_MENU_ICON_NONE for the spare slots; their branches set the
resource ids themselves. The DS text stays under #else and gcc-10 -E -P
without SDK_PORT_3DS is byte-identical (0 diff lines).

